# Bing Bong (kachow) — copy to config/.env and fill in.
# Layering: .env < process environment.

# The Decision Model (ADR 0068) — Jev answers typed questions in ~0.2 s and
# generates nothing. A key alone arms it; the base URL and the pinned model
# id default:
# export TYPESAFE_API_KEY, or set BINGBONG_DECISION_API_KEY, or name the env
# var holding the key with BINGBONG_DECISION_API_KEY_ENV.
# BINGBONG_DECISION_BASE_URL=https://api.typesafe.ai
# BINGBONG_DECISION_MODEL=jev-1.14.0
# The protocol it speaks; one today, /v1/systemone, which any of its hosts
# serves (TypeSafe, Baseten, OpenRouter, TrueFoundry). An unknown value
# leaves the role unconfigured.
# BINGBONG_DECISION_PROTOCOL=systemone
# How long one call may take before it is unavailable (a round's budget):
# BINGBONG_DECISION_TIMEOUT_MS=800
# false for a text-only model: an ask that carries an image (the Mark Ask)
# is then answered unavailable at once instead of sent.
# BINGBONG_DECISION_IMAGES=true
# The Card Budget (ADR 0088), in the host's tokens: every ask, to every model,
# is built to fit it, what is further down on the page yielding first. The
# default is the smallest host the gate asks (Baseten's max_len):
# BINGBONG_DECISION_PROMPT_TOKENS=16384
#
# Another model on the same protocol is env alone. Mammoth-1 on Baseten
# (text-only; p90 ~1.1 s, so the round's 800 ms is too short for it):
# BINGBONG_DECISION_BASE_URL=https://inference.baseten.co
# BINGBONG_DECISION_MODEL=decision-models/baseten-mammoth-27b-latest
# BINGBONG_DECISION_API_KEY_ENV=BASETEN_API_KEY
# BINGBONG_DECISION_IMAGES=false
# BINGBONG_DECISION_TIMEOUT_MS=1500
#
# The corpus gate (`pnpm jev:gate`) asks these models, comma-separated, each
# on the host and key above; a case is through only when every one passes it.
# BINGBONG_GATE_MODELS=decision-models/baseten-mammoth-27b-latest,decision-models/baseten-elephant-9b-latest

# The Story Brief writer (the News card's what-it-is and why-it-matters
# lines) — GLM on Z.ai's coding plan, off the Command path. A key alone
# arms it; the base URL and model default:
# export ZAI_API_KEY, or set BINGBONG_NEWS_WRITER_API_KEY, or name the env
# var holding the key with BINGBONG_NEWS_WRITER_API_KEY_ENV.
# BINGBONG_NEWS_WRITER_BASE_URL=https://api.z.ai/api/coding/paas/v4
# BINGBONG_NEWS_WRITER_MODEL=GLM-5.3

# The scripted stand-in (tests only): a JSON list, one answer per ask —
# {"answers": {…}} or {"unavailable": "<reason>"} — consumed in order.
# BINGBONG_DECISION_SCRIPT=

# The Log Bucket (#418) — the kiosk's log-bucket sidecar (compose.yaml)
# copies <userData>/logs, ask-images included, to a Cloudflare R2 bucket every
# 5 minutes, so the logs outlive the app's 7-day purge and can be read while
# the dev PC is off: `pnpm logs:pull [machine] [dir]` on the dev PC (needs
# rclone, https://rclone.org/install/), then `pnpm perf:report <dir>`. The
# sidecar reads only the BINGBONG_LOG_* and RCLONE_CONFIG_R2_* lines here;
# the model keys above never enter it. Unset, it idles.
#
# Owner steps: create a private bucket that holds only logs, and an R2 API
# token with Object Read & Write on that bucket alone (Cloudflare dashboard ›
# R2 › Manage API tokens). Put the same lines in the kiosk's config/.env and
# the dev PC's root .env. Set a billing notification on the Cloudflare
# account as the backstop: going over the free tier is billed, not blocked.
#
# BINGBONG_LOG_BUCKET=bingbong-logs
# The bucket's folder for this machine; the space check deletes only inside
# it. Compose sets `kiosk` for the sidecar, so this line matters only on
# another machine running docker/log-bucket.sh.
# BINGBONG_LOG_MACHINE=kiosk
# Once a day, over the high mark (the whole bucket, GB), this machine's
# oldest files are deleted until it is under the low mark. The free tier is
# 10 GB-month.
# BINGBONG_LOG_BUCKET_HIGH_GB=8
# BINGBONG_LOG_BUCKET_LOW_GB=7
# The R2 remote, as rclone reads it from the environment:
# RCLONE_CONFIG_R2_TYPE=s3
# RCLONE_CONFIG_R2_PROVIDER=Cloudflare
# RCLONE_CONFIG_R2_ENDPOINT=https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# RCLONE_CONFIG_R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# RCLONE_CONFIG_R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# A token scoped to one bucket may not create or check buckets (compose sets
# this for the sidecar; the dev PC only reads):
# RCLONE_CONFIG_R2_NO_CHECK_BUCKET=true
#
# The sidecar reads these lines when it starts: after filling them in,
# `docker compose restart log-bucket`.
